<ansi fg="black-bold">.:</ansi> <ansi fg="magenta">Help for </ansi><ansi fg="command">prone</ansi>

<ansi fg="red">Prone</ansi> is a combat condition that occurs when you've been knocked to
the ground by special attacks like <ansi fg="command">bash</ansi>,
<ansi fg="command">trip</ansi>, or <ansi fg="command">kick</ansi>.

<ansi fg="yellow">How to Become Prone:</ansi>

  - Hit by a successful <ansi fg="command">bash</ansi> attack
  - Hit by a successful <ansi fg="command">trip</ansi> attack (the most reliable
    knockdown of the three)
  - Hit by a successful <ansi fg="command">kick</ansi> attack

  All knockdown attempts are modified by opposed skill checks — a
  skilled defender is harder to floor than a novice.

<ansi fg="yellow">Effects While Prone:</ansi>

  <ansi fg="red">Attack Penalties:</ansi>
    - Attacking from the ground is substantially harder — both your
      accuracy and the force behind each swing suffer.

  <ansi fg="red">Defense Penalties:</ansi>
    - Dodging while prone is nearly impossible; parrying is awkward;
      blocking still works, though not as well as upright.

  <ansi fg="red">Vulnerability:</ansi>
    - Standing opponents find you a much easier target.

  <ansi fg="red">Restrictions:</ansi>
    - Cannot flee from combat
    - Cannot move to other rooms

<ansi fg="yellow">Recovery:</ansi>

You have two ways to recover from being prone:

  1. <ansi fg="stat">Automatic Recovery:</ansi>
     - After a short delay you automatically attempt to stand each round.
     - Success depends on your Dexterity — nimble characters recover
       faster. Each attempt costs your action for that round.
     - No stamina cost.

  2. <ansi fg="stat">Manual Recovery:</ansi> (<ansi fg="command">help stand</ansi>)
     - Use <ansi fg="command">stand</ansi> for guaranteed success at the
       cost of some stamina.
     - Still uses your action for that round.

<ansi fg="yellow">Strategy:</ansi>

Being prone is dangerous — your opponent gains significant advantages.
Automatic recovery is free (only costs your action), so save stamina
unless you absolutely must get up immediately. High Dexterity characters
recover faster on their own.

<ansi fg="yellow">See Also:</ansi>

